    hints: ['What does one row in your result represent? Your output needs 4 rows with columns: channel, total_revenue.'],
    checkValues: [{ channel: 'paid', total_revenue: '1284.89' }],
    solution: 'SELECT u.channel, SUM(o.subtotal) AS total_revenue\nFROM users u\nJOIN orders o ON u.user_id = o.user_id\nGROUP BY u.channel\nORDER BY total_revenue DESC',
    debrief: 'Paid ($1,284.89) leads, followed by organic ($764.92), referral ($544.93), and email ($249.98). Channels with users who placed zero orders (e.g. organic users 13 and 15) are included via their channel peers — the JOIN from users to orders naturally excludes non-buyers. Important: this is gross subtotal, not net revenue — subtracting discounts and shipping would change the ranking. Two approaches worth knowing: Approach A (this solution) — JOIN users to orders, then GROUP BY u.channel + SUM(o.subtotal). Approach B — subquery: SELECT channel, SUM(revenue) FROM (SELECT u.channel, o.subtotal as revenue FROM users u JOIN orders o ...) GROUP BY channel. Approach A is cleaner and more efficient; Approach B helps when you need to pre-filter or pre-transform the order rows before aggregating. Senior follow-up: "How would you also include channels with zero orders?" — switch to LEFT JOIN from users to orders and handle NULL subtotals with COALESCE(SUM(o.subtotal), 0).\n\n**Forensic trap:** Grouping by o.channel instead of u.channel — the orders table has no channel column, so this throws an error. A subtler trap: joining orders to users (reversed direction) then GROUP BY u.channel computes the same result correctly, but users 13 and 15 (organic, no orders) are now silently included in the organic row — or rather, they are excluded from the JOIN anyway, so the result is identical. The real trap is forgetting the JOIN entirely and trying to GROUP BY a column that only exists in the other table.\n\n**Sanity check:** Confirm 4 rows (paid, organic, referral, email). Verify paid total_revenue = 1284.89. Cross-check organic by summing subtotals for users 1, 4, 6, 10 (organic channel): 89.99+159.99+249.99+79.99+59.99+39.99+89.99+39.99+44.99 = should equal 764.92.',
