    prompt: 'A team member shared this query to count deliveries per courier: SELECT courier_id, COUNT(*) AS deliveries FROM orders GROUP BY courier_id ORDER BY deliveries DESC. The ops lead said the numbers are inflated for some couriers. Identify the bug and write the corrected query. Return courier_id and deliveries (successfully delivered orders only), ordered by deliveries descending.',
